@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:storage] brady-dataset-custody
Preparation MUST verify the enrolled pool and parent dataset GUIDs before creating
only the designated disposable cache dataset. Existing unowned datasets or mount
contents MUST NOT be adopted, overwritten or destroyed. Cache storage failures
MUST NOT stop independently running guests or grant direct guest egress.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] brady-service-privilege
The proxy MUST run under its own UID inside Lilly's network namespace with only
the socket capabilities needed for transparency and marking. Signing credentials
MUST be runtime files. Root storage preparation MUST accept only trusted bounded
configuration and use fixed executable argv, never interpolate a shell command.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:storage] brady-pressure-native-mount-flags
The pressure observer MUST inspect the enrolled parent and cache with their native
mount write flags. Service sandbox remounts MUST NOT be mistaken for host ZFS
policy changes. The observer MUST issue only read-only ZFS inspection commands.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:storage;capacity] brady-pressure-sample-cadence
Each observation MUST take its timestamp before its first ZFS read, so no reported
value predates that timestamp. Samples MUST start on a one-second cadence measured
from the previous start, so a slow sample is not followed by a full idle interval
before the next. Freshness MUST NOT be extended to cover slow samples.
